A||||3||maffthekat||Screeching like a banshie||||8||
Z||000000||maffthekat||04-12-2001||08:47 AM||||Hi all,<BR>I've recently had my drive belt for the AC and alternator replaced on my 84 SE as part of a bigger job (replaced exhaust system). It started off as quiet as a quiet thing, but gradually began to squeek a bit when starting the engine. Recently the squeek has turned into a constant whailing and the temperature needle is all over the place.<P>Does anyone know why this is? Its darn annoying thats for sure and I'm getting complaints from the neighbours - in the NEXT street! ||||reg||8
Z||000001||Tigger||04-12-2001||08:53 AM||||Try to re-tighten the accessory belt.  With it loose, turn the waterpump and alternator by hand to see if the bearings are going bad.  I'm assuming the temp is going all over because the belt is slipping and eventually catching up on the waterpump.<P>Probably good time to replace the belt.<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 04-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||walsh2001||04-12-2001||09:04 AM||||The mounting bolts on the alternator have a tendency to strip, allowing the bolts to loosen. To fix this problem permanently, replace the upper alt. mounting bolt with a longer one and place a nut on the other side. <P>Jason||||reg||1
Z||000003||maffthekat||04-12-2001||09:39 AM||||Thanks Guys... will try your suggestions||||reg||1
